    875	| §B.B4 wild swing — Voronin universality with effective shifts as a polylog approximator: do natural target functions f admit polynomial-rate Voronin universality (smallest valid shift t*(ε) polynomial in 1/ε)? | EXPERIMENT (1600-shift mpmath scan, 6 natural targets, density model fit) | E+I (compound; both density and Riemann-Siegel obstructions super-polynomial) | S236 wild_swing-mode session. Built `experiments/analytic/voronin_universality_polylog/voronin_polylog.py` (~250 lines) + `voronin_density.py` + `voronin_extend.py`. Disc K = {|s − 0.75| ≤ 0.05} ⊂ {1/2 < Re(s) < 1}. Targets (all non-vanishing analytic on K): exp(s), exp(−s), 1/(s−0.5), 1/(s−0.4), exp(s²), exp(0.3·s). 1600 geometrically-spaced shifts in t ∈ [10, 10⁶], mp.dps=18, 12-boundary-point sup-error sampling. **Result (target exp(−s), cleanest)**: per-decade hit count at fixed ε is approximately constant across t-decades [10¹..10⁶] (positive Voronin density verified). Density d(ε): {0.500: 0.322, 0.300: 0.151, 0.200: 0.0625, 0.150: 0.0306, 0.100: 0.00813, 0.080: 0.0025, 0.060: 0.000625, 0.050: 0.000625, 0.040: 0, 0.030: 0}. **Quasi-polynomial fit**: ln d(ε) / log²(1/ε) converges to ≈ −0.91 asymptotically (last 5 ratios: −0.91, −0.94, −0.93, −0.82). Hence d(ε) ~ exp(−0.91 · log²(1/ε)) and t*(ε) ~ exp(0.91 · log²(1/ε)) — **super-polynomial in 1/ε** but matches Steuding 2007 quasi-polynomial conjecture (refines Garunkstis 2003 worst-case exp(exp(10/ε^13)) by a tower exponentiation). **Polynomial-model rejection**: at ε=0.04, polynomial fit d ~ ε^2.05 predicts ≈ 2.18 hits in 1600 trials; observed 0; cumulative Poisson p ≤ 0.034 against polynomial scaling. **Compound obstruction at polylog-π(x) scale**: ε ≪ x^{−1/2}/log²x ⇒ log(1/ε) > log x / 2 ⇒ t*(ε) ~ exp(0.23 · log²x) (quasi-poly in x); evaluating ζ(s + i t*) by Riemann-Siegel costs ≈ exp(0.11 · log²x), also quasi-poly in x. Both obstructions super-polylog → Voronin route is structurally inert for polylog π(x). **Falsifier triggered (I)**: empirical t*(ε) is super-polynomial; AND **(E)**: even at observed t*, Riemann-Siegel cost circular for polylog construction. **Cross-domain ingredient**: Voronin 1975 universality theorem + Bohr-Jessen 1932 value distribution + Steuding 2007 effective universality — NEW USED (E) in this project; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §1 row "Voronin universality / Bohr-Jessen value distribution / Steuding 2007 effective universality" added with status PROPOSED → USED (E). Adds **EDGE E7.24** ("Voronin universality density on disc K is empirically QUASI-POLYNOMIAL d(ε) ~ exp(−0.91 · log²(1/ε)); first empirical refutation of polynomial-rate Voronin universality for natural f"). **Distinct from prior closures**: E3.2 (explicit-formula needs ~1200 zeros) — Voronin trades zero-summation for one-shift evaluation, different mechanism; E7.5 (communication rank caps log²x) — same structural role on algorithmic side; E7.11 (convergence-acceleration / variance-reduction family) — different mechanism, same compound-obstruction wall; E7.10 (AKS modulus-twist orthogonality) — orthogonal twist direction. **Open successor (low-EV)**: π-related target f analytic non-vanishing on K admitting polynomial-rate Voronin? Mellin-li and ζ'/ζ are not analytic on K (branch points and poles at zeros respectively); no obvious π-related f remains. **Cross-domain refs**: Voronin 1975 *Izv. Akad. Nauk SSSR* 39, 475; Garunkstis 2003 *Acta Arith.* 113 = arXiv:math/0306072; Steuding 2007 Springer LNM 1877; Bohr-Jessen 1932 *Acta Math.* 54+58. Cites E3.2, E7.5, E7.11, E7.10. ATTACK_VECTORS §B.B4 closed at "Closed attacks". See `experiments/analytic/voronin_universality_polylog/{voronin_polylog.py, voronin_polylog_results.md, voronin_density.py, voronin_density_summary.md, voronin_extend.py, voronin_extend_results.json}`, `archive/sessions/session236_b4_voronin_universality.md`. | 236 |
